  "claim": "For placement 159 on the 3 x 4 torus in twist 11, three certified configurations (7860857, 7985754, 6433130) have an assignment along an odd class ((2, 1), (0, 1), (1, 2)) on a cyclic cover of 3, 3 or 5 sheets, while none of the 692, 244 or 374 simple cycles of the wall graph passes the criterion of the wall theorem. So every good closed walk visits a wall state twice; the crossing wall of the cover assignment is one, with class (3, 3), (-3, -3) or (-3, -1), and rebuilds an assignment alone. Simple cycles are an incomplete decider for the honeycomb contacts with a free place.",
